    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d369">

                <pb facs="0433" n="1167" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1167"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Taylor to Mr.
                            Olney.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-07-04"><hi rendition="#italic">July 4,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Have you my No. 377? Mora demand made subject of a cabinet meeting, and special
                    committee appointed to consider it and report what <pb facs="0434" n="1168"
                        xml:id="pg1168"/> should be done. Outlook for settlement hopeful. I may be
                    summoned by minister of state any day for promised conference. Generally
                    conceded that Government has power to act, trusting to subsequent legislative
                    ratification. No Cortes probable until next February. The right to pay in
                    Spanish currency without interest probably will be insisted upon. Will you
                    instruct me upon that point and as to how far I may go in pressing the matter in
                    next conference should dilatory tactics be resorted to. For the first time the
                    fact accepted here that something must be done.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Taylor.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
